{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/291696-newbie-question-the-differences-between-arisen-shuankhsen-and-decieved","id":291696,"title":"Newbie Question: The Differences Between Arisen, Shuankhsen, and Decieved","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-24T17:59:44-07:00","id":291696,"title":"Newbie Question: The Differences Between Arisen, Shuankhsen, and Decieved","content":"I'm a late-comer to MtC after years of kicking and screamng, and while the material is fascinating, Mummy is very much a game thick in its own metphysics. Can someone explain precisely what the Arisen/Shuankhsen/Decieved are for me (in tiny words), along with anything else relevent about the occult mechanics and history/faith of Irem? I basically need Mummy For Dummies here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T18:14:25-07:00","id":291709,"title":"","content":"<b>Arisen</b>: The Arisen are mummies following the Judges, ancient pseudo-gods of a lost empire. Their purpose is to retrieve relics imbued with divine life-force, and send them back to the underworld. All Arisen (the Deathless) belong to one of five Guilds, organisations that reflect ancient trade guilds that helped build the Nameless Empire. To aid in their divine task, they form cults around themselves and their Judges using mortals. Each mummy makes a decree to one of the parts of the Egyptian five-part soul (this is the equivalent of Clan or Path in other NWoD games).<br /> <br /> <b>Shuanksen</b>: The Lifeless are mummies that were created when the the guildmasters of the Nameless Empire sacrificed countless slaves to develop the Rite of Return, the powerful spell that created the Arisen. The Shuanksen, rather than serving the Judges, follow the Devourer. Some Shuanksen were once Arisen, but through a variety of ways, they fell from grace.<br /> <br /> <b>Deceived</b>: Members of the lost sixth guild, whose members were artists. Little is known about them, only that they were betrayed by the other five guilds, and none of the Arisen remember why. (Not a lot has been released on the Deceived; their book is coming out soon, though).<br /> <br /> That's all off the top of my head, so people can correct me if I've made any vital errors, or left out anything really important. The core rule book lays things out pretty well, though you have to filter through some of the mythos to get at the basics. Also, depending on if you're a player or an ST, the second half of the core book has background details meant for the Storyteller only. That said, knowing the stuff in the second half hasn't strongly affected my view of the game as a player, so take that with a grain of salt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T18:18:18-07:00","id":291710,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure whether to spoiler this or not, so in deference to the player-storyteller information divide, I'll err on the side of spoiler conservation.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The Arisen are the dead-and-living eternal servants of the Judges of Duat, who labor to secure the holy relics of their people and deliver them in honor of the Duat. Their memory weakens with the weight of ages, due to some quality of the Rite of Return that binds them to service.<br /> <br /> The Shuankhsen are the price paid to create the Arisen, a tithe of eternal slaves paid to the cosmic devourer. Her rite does not weaken their memory, but wounds their eternal soul, leaving them wretched and spiritually starving.<br /> <br /> The Deceived are... well, their book isn't out yet. We know that they are much like the Arisen, that they seem to maintain a greater memory of the ages that birthed them, and that they nurse a vicious grudge which fuels them to turn blasphemously against the rightful Judges of Duat recognized by the Arisen.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T20:46:57-07:00","id":291796,"title":"","content":"Second post already spoils the spoilers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T20:59:45-07:00","id":291805,"title":"","content":"It's the principle of the thing.<br /> <br /> I might take a swing at this later after I read some Guildhalls. For now, The Arisen and the Deceived are like two siblings, with the Deceived being the one who saw what daddy was doing behind the door and got kicked out of the family for it, while the Arisen are, mostly, the blindly obedient, 'good' child. The Shuankhsen are like the dog they both kicked who grew up to be murderous canine people tell stories about now in the neighborhood, who still sharply remembers the two children and relishes the idea of chewing on them most of all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-25-2014, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T22:08:02-07:00","id":291821,"title":"","content":"It's kind of important to note, I feel, that in the player section the information on the Shuankhsen and the Deceived (mostly the Shuankhsen) is a bit different to that in the GM section.<br /> <br /> From the perspective of a player, a Shuankhsen is some kind of feral undead abomination. It's clearly animated by a power similar to the Rite of Return. Most Mummies put their existence down to blasphemous attempts by lesser cultures to mimic the Rite of Return, although it is known that a few Shuankhsen are corrupted Arisen.<br /> <br /> The Deceived, meanwhile, are more like a myth or legend. They're heretical masters of magic, as far as the other guilds are concerned, and may or may not have survived Irem's fall. Some Mummies don't even believe there was a sixth guild. If they do exist though, they are clearly working against the will of the Judges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T23:49:21-07:00","id":291831,"title":"","content":"The Shuankhsen are monsters. They're immortal just like you, but <i>wrong</i>. Where other Arisen are your allies and rivals, Shuankhsen cannot ever be anything other than enemies. They derive power from <i>eating your body</i>. They're less powerful than you, individually, but still immortal. Plus, they know some nasty tricks - claws and jaws and things that make it easier for them to eat you.<br /> The Judges like it if you put them down like the rabid dogs they are.<br /> <br /> The Deceived don't exist. They're a footnote in the history of the Nameless Empire. Just because some Closed Books have a few scrolls on them doesn't make it less of an affront against the will of the Judges of Duat to discuss matters pertaining to the Lost Guild, so you and I should stop talking about them - *thinking* about them - right now. You wouldn't want me to report your inquiry to the Maa-Kep guildmaster, would you?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T00:08:54-07:00","id":291836,"title":"","content":"As for us, we're special. We've been selected by the masters of the first culture ever to exist to serve the divine will of the gods - the Judges of the Underworld - and to keep up its memory and legacy. We serve the will of the gods, reclaiming and protecting what's left of the greatest, oldest culture, giving the gods their due.<br /> <br /> We're special. Never let anyone tell you different.<br /> <br /> Our burden is not an easy one. Time is *never* our friend - when we arise, we do so at the hight of our power, but that power fades quickly. There is always a sense of urgency to our existence, in spite of our immortality. Act quick or fail.<br /> <br /> Our burden is not an easy one. We often arise without recollection of previous lives. Confusion and mental exhaustion - insanity, even, in some cases - are, other than the immortal Judges of Duat, often our only companions in the endless, epic journey of our eternal existences.<br /> <br /> Our burden is not an easy one - this is why the Nameless Empire chose the best they could find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:05:33-07:00","id":294066,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that the Shuankhsen (at least the original ones) got an <i>unbelievably</i> raw deal, probably one of the worst in the NWoD. So yes, they're irredeemable monsters who literally want to eat you, but there's a lot of pathos there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}